{
  "_": "MY BEST REASONED ESTIMATE OF MORROWIND'S PLAY RATES. This is the tunable half of the known-answer test: data/rules-morrowind.json is known exactly and is never touched, so when the test misses, the error is here. Reasoning, rate by rate. TRAVEL: Vvardenfell has no point-to-point fast travel outside the strider/boat/guild-guide network and Mark/Recall, and the network's stops are far from where quests actually send you, so a Morrowind hour is dominated by running. Athletics is +0.02/second running, i.e. 50 seconds of running per point; maxing it from a class start of 35 costs ~2650 points, which is ~37 HOURS of continuous running. The documented answer (Athletics maxed by 50-70 h without grinding) therefore REQUIRES about half of every hour to be spent running - that is not a stretch, it is a description of the game. 10.5 km/h at ~5.6 m/s is 52 % of the hour, and ~1680 km over a full playthrough of a 5x5 km island is what all the back-and-forth actually adds up to. JUMPING: Morrowind players jump more or less constantly while travelling, and Acrobatics is +0.15/jump; ~280 jumps/hour is one every 13 seconds of play, which is what it looks like. COMBAT: fights are frequent (cliff racers) but short, and crucially Morrowind rolls TO-HIT - a miss awards nothing. hitRate below is why this content model can be dense in encounters and still not run away with weapon skills. LOCKS: dungeons, houses and Telvanni towers are full of them; ~9/hour with ~1.8 traps sits a Security-major thief at maximum around hour 110, inside a normal playthrough, which is the documented answer. REPAIRS: Armorer is +0.4 per successful repair, and Morrowind's repair loop is a hammer spammed on every item after every fight - ~75/hour is the honest figure for that verb, not a typo. Sources for the answers being reproduced: UESP Morrowind:Leveling, Morrowind:Skills, Morrowind:Main Quest.",
